Using these inputs, the required helium volume is calculated dynamically. Envelope geometries are then derived for each candidate shape based on this volume. MATLAB is used to evaluate candidate geometries including spherical, cuboid, ellipsoid and balloon-type profiles. This reverses the sequence used in prior studies, where shape constraints were imposed first and lift performance was assessed second (Macias and Lee, 2022).
