3.4 Data Analysis
Experimental results are analysed using comparative and statistical methods. Mean values and standard deviations are calculated across trials for each configuration.
Endurance improvement is quantified as a percentage increase relative to the baseline UAV:
%Δt = ((t_buoyant − t_baseline) / t_baseline) × 100
Measured lift values are compared to theoretical predictions to evaluate the accuracy of the buoyancy model. Observed endurance improvements are then assessed against expected trends based on effective weight reduction.
This analysis allows direct evaluation of whether buoyancy-assisted lift produces measurable improvements in UAV endurance under controlled conditions.
