5. Discussion
Assumptions and Limitations
This study operates under several assumptions to maintain experimental control and reproducibility.
The testing environment is indoor with minimal disturbance. Air density is assumed constant, and helium purity is treated as ideal. Aerodynamic drag effects are not explicitly modelled. The mechanical connection between the UAV and envelope is fixed and not analysed as a variable.
These assumptions limit how broadly the results can be applied, but they help isolate the effects of buoyancy and control. Future work may extend this method to include aerodynamic modelling, outdoor testing, and alternative stabilisation strategies. These limitations reflect the distinction between controlled indoor buoyancy studies and more complex outdoor or application-specific systems reported in the literature (Palossi et al., 2017; Hickson et al.; Macias and Lee, 2022).
